1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,960
 Let us now understand how .NET apps are run in Docker.

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:10,060
 First a Docker container is created.

3
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:18,900
 Next we install an operating system like Windows, Linux, or Mac OS in this container.

4
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:26,140
 Then in this OS we install .NET runtime or SDK.

5
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:29,620
 Next we install a web server like

6
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:34,520
 Apache, Engine X, etc.

7
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:40,160
 Finally a .NET app will run from inside this container.

8
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:52,800
 Since the app has all deleted resources or dependencies like OS.NET runtime as pk web servers

9
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,400
 like Engine X.

10
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:03,160
 So this .NET app is ready to run from inside the Docker container.

11
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:08,200
 Let us understand the working from a real world example.

12
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:13,960
 The boy is opening an ASP.NET Core website on his browser.

13
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:20,040
 First a browser will make an HTTP request to the Engine X web server.

14
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:25,840
 Engine X web server will forward this request to cluster web server.

15
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:31,640
 Note that Engine X is working as a reverse proxy in this case.

16
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:35,480
 Crestale is hosting the .NET web site.

17
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:38,800
 It forwards the request to the web site.

18
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:44,360
 The web site in turn sends back the response to Crestale.

19
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:49,880
 And now Crestale forwards the request to Engine X web server.

20
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:55,160
 Finally, Engine X sends the response to the boy's browser.

21
00:01:55,160 --> 00:02:00,360
 The browser will show the web site.

22
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:08,440
 This whole thing, the Engine X the cluster, the .NET app, is hosted on a Docker container.

23
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:12,800
 Docker is super fast and easy.

24
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:20,080
 Think about installing Windows 11 with .NET SDK on your PC.

25
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:24,880
 It will take no less than one hour of your time.

26
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:32,840
 But in Docker you can install both these things in just 20 to 30 seconds only.

27
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:40,320
 You just have to run the Docker commands and Docker will do the heavy lifting for you.

28
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:47,600
 The Docker commands will tell Docker engine what type of Docker container you need.

29
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:52,640
 Along with the software needed on the container.

30
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:56,240
 This whole process is extremely fast.

31
00:02:56,240 --> 00:03:02,320
 Docker will provide the container running in a matter of seconds.

32
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:06,640
 Create containers of different .NET versions.

33
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:13,360
 For example, a container can be running on Windows along with .NET version 10.

34
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:19,360
 Second container can be running on Linux with .NET 8.0.

35
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:30,200
 Third container can be running on Linux with .NET version 9 along with Node.js and PHP.

36
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:37,600
 These all three containers can run at the same time from the host operating system.

37
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:44,760
 Docker provides these containers all the resources they need for the need.

38
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:55,740
 These includes, required software, like Linux, .NET, Node.js and PHP installed on these

39
00:03:55,740 --> 00:04:06,560
 containers, note that there is no need to install Linux, Node.js .NET or PHP on the host

40
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:15,240
 machine which is our PC as these are running from inside the containers.

41
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:22,440
 Benefits of Docker fast and easy continuous delivery of apps.

42
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:30,340
 Docker is great for continuous integration and continuous delivery of software development.

43
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:33,840
 This is known as CI/CD.

44
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:42,400
 Developers and testers working in a project can share their work using Docker containers.

45
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:51,840
 This developer creates code for a .NET app and pushes the whole app on a Docker container.

46
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:59,880
 The tester will use the container to test the code and will provide the bug list.

47
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:07,480
 This means that Docker container, both the developer and tester are working together.

48
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:16,400
 Once the bug list is resolved, the new .NET app is deployed to the production.

49
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:23,040
 It is not necessary for the developers and testers to remain side by side sitting at the

50
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:28,440
 same office that testers can be anywhere on the world.

51
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:33,000
 They just need to test the app from Docker containers.

52
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:39,240
 In this way, Docker provides very fast and consistent delivery of apps.

53
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:44,880
 Responsive development and scaling of apps with Docker.

54
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:52,280
 For example, we have a .NET website and we noticed a traffic to the website has increased

55
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,760
 by 100%.

56
00:05:53,760 --> 00:06:03,480
 We can increase the Docker containers hosting the website in order to fulfill the new demands.

57
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:16,680
 Earlier, we were hosting the website from 10 containers.

58
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:24,240
 In the same way, we can scale down the app by reducing the containers, thus reducing

59
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:31,840
 the hosting charges of our website, reducing the cost of development of apps when we use

60
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:40,520
 Docker, a small startup has a small team of developers and testers and they do not have

61
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:48,720
 lots of funds to create infrastructure so they can run all the needful apps from the

62
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:50,720
 Docker containers.

63
00:06:50,720 --> 00:07:01,800
 These apps are SQL Server, MySQL, Redis.NET, Node.js, Apache and others.

64
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:08,560
 As reducing the infrastructure cost of the company also, they do not have to shed more

65
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:16,880
 money on buying their license fees when they are running the apps from the Docker containers.

